<LegalPage locale={defaultLocale} title="Editorial Policy" lastUpdated="2026-10-15" description="How we research Chained Beasts guides, distinguish versions and opinions, credit imagery and handle corrections.">
 <p>Our goal is useful, verifiable English guidance. We use official developer announcements, store listings, platform documentation and, when available, current in-game evidence. Public player discussions help identify questions; an unanswered report does not establish a cause or a fix.</p>
 <h2>Facts and recommendations</h2><p>We link factual claims to sources and identify tactical suggestions as editorial advice. Our initial guides are source-based introductions; they are not presented as hands-on testing or completed walkthroughs. We do not invent stats, unlock conditions, controls or comparative rankings.</p>
 <h2>Versions and dates</h2><p>Demo, beta, launch and future roadmap information are distinct. Historical details are labeled, and a development target is not described as a released feature. Article dates reflect publication and actual review rather than an automatically refreshed timestamp.</p>
 <h2>Community evidence and troubleshooting</h2><p>We identify developer replies separately from player observations. A community answer, even one marked as accepted, is not automatically an official statement. We identify the relevant version and link to the original discussion when using community evidence. General Steam or console troubleshooting is labeled as platform guidance; it is not presented as a tested fix for a Chained Beasts issue.</p>
 <h2>Original writing and imagery</h2><p>Articles synthesize information in our own words. Game screenshots are sourced from official promotional material and remain the property of their rights holders. We do not use AI-generated game imagery.</p>
 <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Report an error through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, including the affected statement and supporting evidence. We revise the article and its review date when the substance changes. Material corrections are noted in the article.</p>
 <h2>Advertising and independence</h2><p>Advertising is labeled and does not determine guide recommendations. We are not affiliated with Featherweight Games. Paid ads are distinct from official store links and editorial navigation.</p>
</LegalPage>
